{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "6c1f2e8a-4b7d-4c39-9f0e-2a8d5b3c7e18",
    "name": "Bug Tracking System A2",
    "description": "Syed's hand-over for the master collection (Postman Shared Workspace Guide): folder **03 Notifications FR-2/NFR-2**. Avinandan: drag that folder into the master collection after 02 Audit. The 00 Auth folder here is only a copy so this file runs on its own; the master already has it.\n\n**Notifications (FR-2):** a fresh bug is reported, claimed, resolved and re-opened, checking who is notified at each step (claim → reporter; resolve → reporter and QA Leads; re-open → assigned developer), plus listing own notifications, mark read, and the 401/404 error cases.\n\n**Rate limit (NFR-2):** all POST, PATCH and PUT requests under /api are limited to **60 per minute per client IP**. Once the limit is reached the API returns 429 with { \"success\": false, \"errors\": [\"Too many requests, please try again in a minute.\"] }. GET requests are not limited. Behind the ALB the client IP comes from X-Forwarded-For (app.set('trust proxy', 1)). Counts are kept per server instance, so through the ALB (two instances) the effective limit is about 120 per minute: set the instances variable to 2 in the ALB environment.\n\nWait at least a minute between full runs: the rate-limit request uses up the limit for your IP, and the next run's logins would get 429.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
